{"id":"neet-2025-q087","pn":87,"y":"NEET 2025","tp":"Chemical Bonding and Molecular Structure","st":"Properties: dipole moment, bond order, lone pairs","q":"Identify the correct orders against the property mentioned\nA. H₂O > NH₃ > CHCl₃ – dipole moment\nB. XeF₄ > XeO₃ > XeF₂ – number of lone pairs on central atom\nC. O–H > C–H > N–O – bond length\nD. N₂ > O₂ > H₂ – bond enthalpy\nChoose the correct answer from the options given below:","o":["A, D only","B, D only","A, C only","B, C only"],"c":0,"s":"A. Dipole moment μ (D): H₂O 1.85, NH₃ 1.47, CHCl₃ 1.04. Order H₂O > NH₃ > CHCl₃ is correct.\nB. XeF₄ has 2 lone pairs, XeO₃ has 1 lone pair, XeF₂ has 3 lone pairs. The given order is wrong.\nC. Correct order of bond length: N–O > C–H > O–H. The given order is wrong.\nD. Bond order: N₂ is 3, O₂ is 2, H₂ is 1. So the bond enthalpy order N₂ > O₂ > H₂ is correct."}
